component SigilProjectionStore {
  goal {
    Publish disposable source-bound assertions without accepting stale or
    out-of-order reconstruction as current evidence.
  }

  interface {
    CurrentImplementation {
      Select arbitrary-language source files and assemble only fresh indexed
      assertions against the current frozen Design catalog. Validate resource
      identity again on reading and enforce aggregate assertion limits before
      closure. Keep the catalog out of Implementation evidence.
      Saturate in an independent EGraph and identify the captured selection,
      catalog and assertion contents. Missing sources and completed empty facts
      remain distinct. Explicit empty selection is visible in the report.
    }

    DesignCommands {
      Expose prepare, ingest, stale and compile for Design and entities for its
      catalog. Accept an explicit frontend bundle and workspace root. Preparation
      writes only bound Design context, fixed ontology and a job descriptor into
      a new caller-selected directory; refuse to overwrite existing directories.
      Ingestion checks the job source and current inputs before publication.
      Report completed Loose or Disjoint with exit one, invalid options with two,
      and operational failure without a semantic result with three.
      No provider, model or automatic repair options exist.
    }

    CurrentDesign {
      Assemble fresh source projections against a recaptured frontend snapshot.
      Add only structural type and label facts plus required unit inventory from
      the frontend. Missing projections leave Design Loose unless fresh facts
      already establish Disjoint. Frontend errors produce no completed verdict.
      Validate the complete identity set before freezing a current catalog.
      Reports identify captured inputs, projection contents and compiled kernel.
      Prepare Design context only from its bound source and dependency closure.
    }

    ProjectionPublication {
      Capture the expected per-source generation before reconstruction.
      Under one OS file lock, compare the prepared binding and generation with
      current inputs and recheck source and Design dependency bytes. Publish
      bounded data-only assertions by temporary-file replacement, then atomically
      replace the index that binds their checksum to inputs and generation.
      Reject duplicate jobs and changed source, catalog or format inputs.
      Keep scheduling, workers and production metadata outside the store.
    }

    IndexedAssembly {
      Mirror normalized source paths with their original extensions plus egg.
      Load only index-selected assertions with matching complete input bindings
      and checksums. Parse them as restricted data. Missing, stale, corrupt,
      deleted and unindexed objects contribute no current facts.
      Bound index and assertion bytes separately. Refuse path traversal,
      symlinked artifact paths and malformed index metadata.
      A busy writer lock is an operational failure, never a semantic result.
    }
  }
}
